{title: I Fear You}
{artist: Jeff Deyo}
{key: F}
{tempo: 170}

{comment: Intro}
[Gm]  [Dm]  [C]

{comment: Verse 1}
I [Dm]humble [Bb]myself [F]before You   [C]
I [Dm]lay [Bb]myself down [F]below You   [C]
In [Dm]revere[Bb]nce I bow  [F]   [C]
Beneath [G]You, my Lord[Bb]

{comment: Verse 2}
I [Dm]draw [Bb]near to You [F]forever   [C]
My [Dm]Savior,[Bb] my God, [F]my treasure   [C]
I [Dm]stand [Bb]here in awe[F]    [C]
Indebted [G]to You, my [Bb]Lord

{comment: Chorus}
Cause I [F]fear You,[C] my [Bb]God
And I [F]fear You, [C]my King[Bb]
And I [F]trust You [C]with my [Bb]soul
And I [Gm]love You with all my [C]heart
And I [Gm]fear You with all my [C]life

{comment: Verse 3}
I [Dm]feel [Bb]like a child [F]around [C]You
As [Dm]I let [Bb]all my [F]praise [C]surround You
And [Dm]I [Bb]fall on my [F]face       [C]
Astounded[G], my Lord [Bb]

{comment: Bridge}
You hold the [Bb]oceans within Your [C]hand
You count the [Bb]galaxies      [C]
You know the [Bb]mysteries of this [C]world
You see [Gm]what no one [C]sees
Your hand can [Bb]span the whole [C]universe
You gave the [Bb]stars their fame   [C]
You know my [Bb]deepest of secrets, [C]Lord
But still you [Gm]have called me by [C]name, still you have called me by name
